Intel inherited display startup: register and sequence adaptations

Pinned reference: Linux v6.19, commit
05f7e89ab9731565d8a62e3b5d1ec206485eeb0b.
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/tree/05f7e89ab9731565d8a62e3b5d1ec206485eeb0b/drivers/gpu/drm

Adapted subset: i915/display/intel_display_power_well.c DC-state settling and
additive BIOS-held power-well requests; intel_display_regs.h,
skl_universal_plane_regs.h, intel_cursor_regs.h and intel_vdsc_regs.h numeric
register definitions; xe/xe_ggtt.c inherited raw-PTE read layout.

Local changes: matched-profile startup, retained inherited request ownership,
read-only configuration/GGTT mappings, a two-register control write boundary,
bounded observations and uncertain-cleanup retention. No Linux power manager,
DMC firmware loader, modesetting, interrupt programming or BO manager is imported.
No upstream source is fetched by the build.

